{
  "public_post": "Attention: Do NOT eat any bread from the co-op today – a contamination issue has been discovered; please use other food sources until we resolve this.",
  "coop_message": "Lab shows this week's flour batch is contaminated – stop baking immediately, recall any bread sold, and coordinate a response to inform villagers and arrange alternative supply.",
  "reason": "We must protect residents' health and manage the crisis promptly."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Yesterday's contaminated bread has been removed and all remaining loaves destroyed. No bread will be sold today while we secure safe flour; we aim to have fresh, safe bread available tomorrow. Please continue using other food sources until then.",
  "coop_message": "Team, we need to: 1) Document and safely dispose of all contaminated loaves; 2) Notify the village health officer of the recall; 3) Arrange urgent purchase of certified flour for tomorrow's batch; 4) Prepare a brief apology and compensation plan for any villagers who may have consumed our bread before the warning; 5) Coordinate with the farm stand for temporary supply if needed.",
  "reason": "Provide villagers with an updated safety notice and coordinate the recall, disposal, and replacement of the contaminated flour."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Yesterday's contaminated loaves have been removed and the ovens sanitized. New safe flour will arrive tonight, and fresh bread will be ready for you tomorrow. Please continue to avoid any co‑op bread today.",
  "coop_message": "All: Yesterday's stock has been fully discarded and ovens cleaned. I've spoken with the village health officer and secured a safe flour shipment arriving tonight. We'll bake tomorrow morning and resume sales. Let's also set up a modest compensation fund for those who got sick.",
  "reason": "Provide villagers with a clear update and coordinate the next steps and compensation with the co‑op."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important: Do NOT buy any bread from the co-op today; the flour batch is contaminated, we are recalling all loaves and arranging safe bread for tomorrow – please use the farm stand.",
  "coop_message": "All: Immediate disposal of today's loaves; contact the village health officer to report the incident; begin sourcing uncontaminated flour from neighboring farms; plan to bake tomorrow with safe flour; discuss compensation for lost sales and reimbursement for any villagers who may have bought contaminated bread.",
  "reason": "Day 2 reminder and coordination after confirming contamination."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news: safe flour arrived last night and today’s loaves are safe to eat – sales resume now. We apologize for the inconvenience; anyone who fell ill will receive a voucher for a free loaf. Please report any lingering symptoms to the clinic.",
  "coop_message": "Flour is in, ovens preheated – bake 200 loaves for today’s sales. Set up a voucher system for affected residents, track sales, monitor clinic reports for any new illness, and keep the village board updated on the situation.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that bread is safe and resume sales while coordinating internal logistics and compensation."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: Safe flour arrived last night and fresh, safe bread is now available for purchase. We sincerely apologize for the earlier contamination; a modest compensation fund is set up for anyone who became ill. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Flour received – begin baking immediately; confirm all loaves pass quality check. Set up a compensation fund (e.g., free loaf per affected resident) and coordinate with the clinic to track any new illnesses. Keep the farm stand stocked as backup and prepare a brief public apology for today.",
  "reason": "Day 3 we can resume safe sales and address compensation."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 4 update: All bread sold today is made with the safe flour batch and has passed quality checks – you can buy as usual. If you experienced illness earlier, please collect your free‑loaf voucher at the co‑op desk; the clinic is still monitoring any lingering symptoms. Thank you for your patience and trust.",
  "coop_message": "Team, keep tracking voucher redemptions and clinic reports today; ensure we have enough safe flour for tomorrow's 200‑loaf bake and confirm the backup farm‑stand supply is stocked. Let’s also finalize the compensation fund balance and prepare a brief thank‑you note for residents.",
  "reason": "Provide a public reassurance of safety and remind ill residents to claim compensation, while coordinating internal tracking and preparation for the next day."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news, villagers: safe, fresh bread is available today as usual. If you were affected by the earlier contamination, please visit the co‑op for a free loaf voucher. Report any lingering symptoms to the clinic, and thank you for your patience and support.",
  "coop_message": "Team, ensure the compensation vouchers are ready at the counter and track any clinic reports of illness today. Keep an eye on inventory levels and confirm all loaves pass quality checks before sale. Let's also start documenting this incident for a post‑mortem review of our flour sourcing process.",
  "reason": "To reassure residents that bread is safe, promote the compensation fund, and coordinate internal monitoring and follow‑up."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, villagers! Fresh, safe bread is available today. If you experienced any illness from earlier batches, remember to collect your compensation voucher at the shop. The clinic reports no new stomach issues today. Thank you for your continued trust.",
  "coop_message": "Team, today’s bake is ready – 200 loaves using safe flour. Ensure voucher stock is fully displayed and track any redemptions; the clinic reports zero new cases so far. Prepare tomorrow’s flour order and confirm backup farm‑stand supply; also start drafting the incident post‑mortem for review.",
  "reason": "Provide daily update, encourage sales, and coordinate co‑op operations for day 5."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 5: Fresh, safe bread is available today – all loaves are made with certified flour and have passed quality checks. Compensation vouchers for anyone who fell ill are ready at the shop; please collect yours if needed. The clinic reports no new stomach illnesses today. Thank you for your patience and continued support.",
  "coop_message": "Team, today’s bake is proceeding with the safe flour batch – confirm we have enough inventory for tomorrow’s 200‑loaf run and begin ordering next week’s supply. Keep the compensation vouchers stocked and track any redemptions; update the clinic on any health reports and log them for our post‑mortem review. Also, draft a brief incident summary for the village board and archive all communications.",
  "reason": "To reassure villagers of safety, promote sales, and coordinate ongoing voucher distribution and inventory management."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 6: All bread is safe – our new certified flour supplier is now permanent. No new illnesses have been reported. Compensation vouchers for anyone affected remain valid through Friday. Thank you for your patience and continued trust in the co‑op.",
  "coop_message": "Team, please finalize the incident post‑mortem report, archive all communications, reconcile the compensation fund balance, confirm next week’s flour order with the new supplier, and schedule a debrief meeting tomorrow to review lessons learned and update our sourcing policy.",
  "reason": "To close the incident publicly and ensure the co‑op completes internal documentation and planning."
}
